  "Question": "In a mathematics contest with ten problems, a student gains \\(5\\) points for a correct answer and loses \\(2\\) points for an incorrect answer. If Olivia answered every problem and her score was \\(29,\\) how many correct answers did she have?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(5\\)",
    "B": "\\(6\\)",
    "C": "\\(7\\)",
    "D": "\\(8\\)",
    "E": "\\(9\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "If all ten answers were correct, Olivia would score \\(10\\cdot5=50\\) points. Changing one correct answer to an incorrect answer removes the \\(5\\) points and adds a \\(2\\)-point penalty, lowering the score by \\(5+2=7\\) points. Her score is \\(50-29=21\\) points below perfect, so she had \\(21\\div7=3\\) incorrect answers. She therefore had \\(10-3=7\\) correct answers. Indeed, \\(7\\cdot5-3\\cdot2=29\\), so the answer is \\(7\\), choice \\(\\text{C}\\).",
